.TH LITESITE 1 "May 2026" "litesite 2.4.0"
.SH NAME
litesite \- create and work with tiny static sites
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B litesite
[\fB-C\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B litesite
works on a site root that contains \fBsrc/\fR, \fB.deploy-filter\fR,
\fBjustfile\fR, and \fB.editorconfig\fR.

It can build the site into \fBdist/\fR, serve the public directory, deploy the
output with \fBrsdeploy\fR, regenerate compressed assets and AVIF JPG/WebP
derivatives, expand SSI-style file includes in HTML files, or scaffold a new
site.

When no command is supplied,
.B litesite
runs the usage screen
.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Build \fBdist/\fR from \fBsrc/\fR, expand SSI-style HTML file includes unless
disabled, minify HTML/CSS/JS unless disabled, copy public assets, generate
sibling \fB*.avif.jpg\fR and \fB*.avif.webp\fR derivatives, and write
compressed Brotli, gzip, and zstd variants.
.TP
.B clean
Remove \fBdist/\fR.
.TP
.B serve
Run a local preview server against \fBsrc/public/\fR with Tornado-style log
prefixes and SSE live reload. CSS changes hot-swap stylesheets in place, other
watched file changes reload the page, and browser tabs reconnect across server
restarts.
.TP
.B deploy
Build the site and deploy \fBdist/\fR. Pass \fB-n\fR to preview a dry-run
deployment. \fBrsdeploy\fR is required for this command.
.TP
.B compress
Regenerate Brotli, gzip, and zstd files for \fBdist/\fR.
.TP
.B media
Regenerate sibling \fB*.avif.jpg\fR and \fB*.avif.webp\fR derivatives in
\fBdist/\fR.
.TP
.B new [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fISLUG\fR [\fIDEST\fR]
Create a new site scaffold.
.TP
.B init [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fISLUG\fR [\fIDEST\fR]
Alias for \fBnew\fR.
.TP
.B jpg \fIFILES...\fR
Convert AVIF files to JPG beside the source path.
.TP
.B webp \fIFILES...\fR
Convert AVIF files to WebP beside the source path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -C \fIDIR\fR
Run against another site root.
.TP
.B -h
Show help.
.TP
.B -v
Show version.
.TP
.B -t \fINAME-OR-PATH\fR, --template \fINAME-OR-PATH\fR
Select the Mustache template used by \fBnew\fR or \fBinit\fR. Template names
resolve as built-ins first, then from \fB.litesite/templates/\fR and
\fB.config/litesite/templates/\fR in the current directory or a parent, then
from \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/litesite/templates/\fR or
\fB$HOME/.config/litesite/templates/\fR, then as an explicit path.
.TP
.B --var \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Add a string variable to the selected template. This option may be repeated.
Later options override earlier values.
.TP
.B --vars \fIFILE.json\fR
Load string variables from a JSON object. Later options override earlier
values.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LITESITE_BUILD_BROTLI
Set to \fB0\fR, \fBfalse\fR, \fBno\fR, or \fBoff\fR to skip Brotli output.
.TP
.B LITESITE_BUILD_GZIP
Set to \fB0\fR, \fBfalse\fR, \fBno\fR, or \fBoff\fR to skip gzip output.
.TP
.B LITESITE_BUILD_ZSTD
Set to \fB0\fR, \fBfalse\fR, \fBno\fR, or \fBoff\fR to skip zstd output.
.TP
.B LITESITE_BUILD_INCLUDES
Set to \fB0\fR, \fBfalse\fR, \fBno\fR, or \fBoff\fR to skip HTML file includes.
.TP
.B LITESITE_BUILD_MINIFY
Set to \fB0\fR, \fBfalse\fR, \fBno\fR, or \fBoff\fR to skip HTML/CSS/JS
minification.
.TP
.B LITESITE_BUILD_AVIF_JPEG
Set to \fB0\fR, \fBfalse\fR, \fBno\fR, or \fBoff\fR to skip JPG derivative generation.
.TP
.B LITESITE_BUILD_AVIF_WEBP
Set to \fB0\fR, \fBfalse\fR, \fBno\fR, or \fBoff\fR to skip WebP derivative generation.
.SH NOTES
When \fBnew\fR or \fBinit\fR is called without \fIDEST\fR, the new site is
created as \fB./\fISLUG\fR\fR.
.PP
Template files ending in \fB.mustache\fR are rendered and written without the
suffix. Paths may contain \fB[slug]\fR, matching comprose's path placeholder
format, and may use any variable passed with \fB--var\fR or \fB--vars\fR.
Templates receive those variables for Mustache rendering as well as default
\fBslug\fR, \fByear\fR, and \fBauthor\fR values. Only \fBslug\fR is
reserved. \fByear\fR defaults to the current year; \fBauthor\fR defaults to a
local Git repository author, then \fBwhoami\fR, then \fBYour Name\fR. Either
may be overridden by template or command-line variables.
.PP
A template may contain a root \fB.litesite.json\fR file with default string
variables in its \fBvars\fR object. These values load before command-line
variables and are never copied into the generated site.
